# netsurf: a late image re-lays out only its own lines (incremental reflow)
#
# Roadmap WS-C item 2 part B. An object that arrives after the page is
# laid out (patch 162's lazy drain, a slow server) cost a full
# layout_document of the whole page each time a batch landed -- 50-75 ms
# on the host for a 5000-paragraph page, several hundred ms on the Vita,
# while the user scrolls.
#
# - layout.c: layout_relayout_object() lays out again only the object's
#   inline container (or, for an image that is display: block, the block
#   itself), moves every later sibling of every ancestor down by the change
#   in height, grows the ancestors and refreshes their descendant bboxes.
#   It says no -- the caller does the full reflow -- whenever the result
#   could differ from a full layout: floats in the formatting context,
#   inline-blocks or positioned boxes in the line, an ancestor that is not
#   a plain auto-height block (table, flex, grid, float, abs, multicol,
#   min/max height, list marker), margin collapsing that changes (the
#   HAS_HEIGHT / MAKE_HEIGHT flags from the min/max pass, which it redoes
#   as layout_document would), an absolutely positioned box offset from a
#   containing block outside what moves, a fixed box, iframes, a page
#   shorter than the screen. layout_relayout_why names the reason.
# - html.c: html_relayout_object_local() runs it on a DONE page, updates
#   the page size as html_reformat does and tells the window from the
#   scheduler (html_relayout_notify: inside the object's broadcast a nested
#   REFORMAT is dropped). html_reformat logs each full layout's duration
#   ("LIFE reformat #N: layout M ms") and clears late_reflow_pending.
# - object.c: the three places that reflowed the whole page for a late
#   object try the local relayout first; the guaranteed reflow at
#   active==0 is skipped for an object already placed, one sized by CSS
#   (REPLACE_DIM: nothing moved) or one only starting to load, unless a
#   full reflow is still owed (late_reflow_pending, private.h).
# Sim, JS-reflow-stall.html (4 dimensionless images arriving at the bottom
# of 5000 paragraphs): local relayouts 6-14 us each; longest main-loop
# gap 38-40 ms (the rest of the object callbacks) instead of 98-109 ms;
# every position identical to a full layout's (checked element by element
# with the local path switched off). A display: block image with no size
# is an empty block that margins collapse through, so it still takes the
# full path when it arrives.
